OpenJPEG's licence and notices
==============================

neo-j2k's libraries (neoj2k.dll, libneoj2k.so and the static libraries) contain code ported from
OpenJPEG (https://github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg), through the fork it is based on
(https://github.com/anne-skydancer/openjpeg): src/image.cpp and src/defaults.cpp, from OpenJPEG's
image.c and openjpeg.c; the declarations of include/neoj2k/neoj2k.h, from openjpeg.h; the header
checks and messages of src/header.cpp and src/jp2.cpp, from j2k.c and jp2.c; the header read's image,
codestream information and messages of src/codec.cpp, from j2k.c and openjpeg.c; the stream of
src/stream.cpp, from cio.c and openjpeg.c; and the decoder: src/decode.cpp from j2k.c, src/tile.cpp
from tcd.c, src/t2.cpp from pi.c, bio.c, tgt.c and t2.c, src/t1.cpp from t1.c, mqc.c, mqc_inl.h and
t1_luts.h, src/dwt.cpp from dwt.c, and src/mct.cpp from mct.c and tcd.c. OpenJPEG is licensed
under the BSD 2-Clause License, whose second clause asks for its notice in binary distributions
too. Its licence, as OpenJPEG's LICENSE file gives it, follows; the ported files carry these notices
as well:

